  "versionNotes": [
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.34 Pod-level resources and v1.37 resource managers",
      "items": [
        "The .spec.resources CPU/memory/hugepages API is Beta since Kubernetes v1.34 and enabled by default upstream in v1.37. The distinct Pod-level resource managers feature is Beta since v1.37 but disabled by default; it needs the PodLevelResourceManagers gate on relevant components and lets CPU, memory, and topology managers use Pod-level declarations for allocation decisions. Do not conflate API availability with manager integration or describe either as Stable."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.37 current stable release",
      "items": [
        "The official release page lists v1.37.1 (released 2026-09-15) as the latest release as checked 2026-11-20. Notable workload-facing changes: metrics.k8s.io graduates to the stable v1 API (v1beta1 remains usable during migration); HPA scale-to-zero for suitable object/external metrics is Beta and enabled by default; gang scheduling and workload-aware preemption graduate to Beta; Dynamic Resource Allocation (DRA) adds stable extended-resource support, device taints/tolerations, and standardized device status/NUMA information. Verify the cluster version, feature status, and component support before relying on a feature."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/releases/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/08/26/kubernetes-v1-37-release/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/09/02/kubernetes-v1-37-hpa-scale-to-zero-beta/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/09/03/kubernetes-v1-37-dra-updates/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.35 in-place Pod resize",
      "items": [
        "In-place CPU and memory resize became stable in v1.35. The Pod /resize subresource adjusts a running Pod's container requests and limits; resizePolicy determines whether a container restart is required. This changes an existing Pod and should not be confused with editing a workload template, which triggers replacement Pods."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/configuration/manage-resources-containers/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/configure-pod-container/resize-container-resources/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.36 user namespaces",
      "items": [
        "Pod user namespaces became Stable in Kubernetes v1.36. A Linux Pod opts in with spec.hostUsers=false, mapping container identities to distinct host identities; runtime, filesystem, host namespace, and storage limitations still apply."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/04/23/kubernetes-v1-36-userns-ga/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/user-namespaces/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.34 and v1.36 storage APIs",
      "items": [
        "VolumeAttributesClass reached GA in Kubernetes v1.34 and its feature gate was locked in v1.36. Kubernetes v1.36 also made OCI image volume sources and VolumeGroupSnapshot support Stable. These features still depend on CSI drivers, the snapshot controller, compatible storage APIs, and backend support; group snapshots are crash-consistent rather than automatically application-consistent."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2025/09/08/kubernetes-v1-34-volume-attributes-class/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volume-attributes-classes/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/storage/volumes/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/04/22/kubernetes-v1-36-release/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/blog/2026/05/08/kubernetes-v1-36-volume-group-snapshot-ga/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.33 sidecar containers",
      "items": [
        "SidecarContainers became stable in Kubernetes v1.33; restartable sidecars are represented as init containers with container-level restartPolicy Always. The sidecar feature gate had been enabled by default since v1.29, so distinguish default availability from stable status."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/sidecar-containers/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/"
      ]
    },
    {
      "edition": "Kubernetes v1.31 PodDisruptionBudget unhealthy pod eviction policy",
      "items": [
        "The unhealthyPodEvictionPolicy feature became stable in v1.31; AlwaysAllow can let node drains evict unhealthy Pods that would otherwise block behind the default IfHealthyBudget behavior."
      ],
      "sourceUrls": [
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/tasks/run-application/configure-pdb/",
        "https://kubernetes.io/docs/concepts/workloads/pods/disruptions/"
      ]
    }
  ],
